meta {
  name: 00 How to set a student tier
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/centers/me/students
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  Not a test — the setup every request in this folder depends on, and a place
  to read the current tiers back.

  Each student row carries `tier`. It decides what that student may do, which
  is the second and narrower entitlement question: Phase 5 asked whether a
  center's students may learn at all, and tiers ask what THIS student may do.
  Two students in the same center, both fully paid, can now get different
  answers.

  ## Setting one up

  The supported way is `Center Students / 04 Update student` with
  `{"tier": "PRO"}`, which checks that a free seat exists in the target tier.

  For testing the student-facing gates you often want a tier without buying
  seats, so by hand:

      -- give the center seats to hold
      INSERT INTO center_seats (id, center_id, tier, quantity, unit_price_xaf)
      VALUES (gen_random_uuid()::text, '<center>', 'PRO', 5, 10000);

      -- and put a student in that tier
      UPDATE students SET tier = 'PRO' WHERE id = '<student>';

  ## The three cases the gates distinguish

  | student | tier | governed by a center |
  |---|---|---|
  | a center's Start student | START | yes |
  | a center's Pro student | PRO | yes |
  | an independent student | NULL | no |

  That third row is the one to keep in mind. An independent student — anyone
  who predates centers, or whom a center removed — has no tier, and the two
  gates treat them DIFFERENTLY on purpose:

  - the exam module admits them, because they have it today and taking it away
    would be a regression for a reason that has nothing to do with them;
  - the AI quota meters them at Start's allowance, because nobody is paying
    for those calls and leaving them unmetered would let a center release its
    students to hand them unlimited AI.

  The unifying rule: they keep every FEATURE they have, and unpaid AI runs at
  the floor rate.

  To make one: `UPDATE students SET center_id = NULL WHERE id = '<student>';`
  Note the tier column survives that — see `02 Exam module` for why that
  matters.
}
